{"step_index":463,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-17T11:50:58Z","thinking":"Inventory file `inventory/hosts.ini` defines a local connection. Ad-hoc commands can target hosts specified with inline syntax or inventory files. Considering the task of auditing web certificates, a production-grade playbook seems appropriate. `playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml` appears to be a suitable name for the playbook. A CLI helper might not be needed if the playbook is the primary artifact.\n\n\nConsidering the prompt, the primary focus is auditing web server certificates, requiring installation and activity checks for relevant services. The logic will need to robustly identify and extract certificate details from Nginx and Apache configurations. A fallback mechanism is needed for parsing Nginx configuration files when direct command execution fails.\n\n\nParsing web server configuration files is required to extract virtual host details, including listening ports, certificate paths, and associated key file paths. Subsequently, each identified certificate will undergo validation. This involves checking for file existence, then extracting subject, issuer, expiry date, and subject alternative names. Expiry status is then calculated for each certificate.\n\nA structured JSON output will be constructed, encompassing the installation and activity status of Nginx and Apache, along with their versions and virtual host configurations. The output will also include an overall summary of total virtual hosts, certificates, and discovered domains. This will then be output for use with Ansible.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > /home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml\n---\n# ==============================================================================\n# Playbook: Audit Web Servers (Nginx / Apache / HTTPD) & TLS Certificates\n# ==============================================================================\n# Phase 1: Bootstraps passwordless SSH & sudo for user 'koby-bowser-ansible'\n#          via playbooks/bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml.\n# Phase 2: Audits installed and active web servers (nginx, apache2, httpd).\n#          If one of them is active:\n#            - Extracts all hosted domains (server_name, ServerName, ServerAlias)\n#            - Extracts TLS certificate and private key paths\n#            - Inspects certificate validity (Subject, Issuer, Expiry date, SANs)\n#            - Displays structured per-host reports and a consolidated summary table\n#\n# Usage:\n#   # Audit a single host with initial admin credentials (bootstraps + audits):\n#   ansible-playbook -i \"172.30.39.153:30,\" playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml -u superuser -k -K\n#\n#   # Audit hosts already bootstrapped (using koby-bowser-ansible / id_ed25519):\n#   ansible-playbook -i \"172.30.39.153:30,\" playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml -u koby-bowser-ansible\n#\n#   # Audit an entire inventory group:\n#   ansible-playbook -i inventory/hosts.ini playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml\n# ==============================================================================\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Phase 1: Bootstrap passwordless SSH & sudo\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- name: \"Phase 1 - Bootstrap passwordless SSH & sudo\"\n  ansible.builtin.import_playbook: bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Phase 2: Audit Web Servers & TLS Certificates\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n- name: \"Phase 2 - Audit Web Servers & TLS Certificates\"\n  hosts: all\n  gather_facts: true\n  become: true\n  become_method: ansible.builtin.sudo\n  vars:\n    ansible_ssh_common_args: \"-o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new\"\n\n  tasks:\n    - name: Audit web servers (Nginx/Apache) and TLS certificates via Python engine\n      ansible.builtin.command:\n        argv:\n          - python3\n          - -c\n          - |\n            import subprocess, re, os, json, datetime, shutil\n\n            def inspect_cert(cert_path):\n                if not cert_path or not os.path.isfile(cert_path):\n                    return {\"path\": cert_path, \"exists\": False, \"status\": \"FILE NOT FOUND\"}\n                try:\n                    cmd = [\"openssl\", \"x509\", \"-in\", cert_path, \"-noout\", \"-subject\", \"-issuer\", \"-enddate\"]\n                    out = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n                    subject, issuer, enddate_str = \"\", \"\", \"\"\n                    for line in out.splitlines():\n                        if line.startswith(\"subject=\"):\n                            subject = line.replace(\"subject=\", \"\").strip()\n                        elif line.startswith(\"issuer=\"):\n                            issuer = line.replace(\"issuer=\", \"\").strip()\n                        elif line.startswith(\"notAfter=\"):\n                            enddate_str = line.replace(\"notAfter=\", \"\").strip()\n\n                    days_left = None\n                    status = \"UNKNOWN\"\n                    if enddate_str:\n                        try:\n                            dt = datetime.datetime.strptime(enddate_str, \"%b %d %H:%M:%S %Y %Z\").replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)\n                            now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\n                            days_left = (dt - now).days\n                            if days_left < 0:\n                                status = f\"EXPIRED ({abs(days_left)} days ago)\"\n                            elif days_left < 30:\n                                status = f\"EXPIRING SOON ({days_left} days left)\"\n                            else:\n                                status = f\"VALID ({days_left} days left)\"\n                        except Exception:\n                            status = \"PARSE ERROR\"\n\n                    sans_out = subprocess.run([\"openssl\", \"x509\", \"-in\", cert_path, \"-noout\", \"-ext\", \"subjectAltName\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n                    sans = []\n                    for line in sans_out.splitlines():\n                        if \"DNS:\" in line:\n                            for p in line.split(\",\"):\n                                if \"DNS:\" in p:\n                                    sans.append(p.strip().replace(\"DNS:\", \"\"))\n\n                    return {\n                        \"path\": cert_path,\n                        \"exists\": True,\n                        \"subject\": subject,\n                        \"issuer\": issuer,\n                        \"expires\": enddate_str,\n                        \"days_remaining\": days_left,\n                        \"status\": status,\n                        \"sans\": sans\n                    }\n                except Exception as e:\n                    return {\"path\": cert_path, \"exists\": False, \"error\": str(e), \"status\": \"ERROR\"}\n\n            def parse_nginx():\n                res = {\"installed\": False, \"active\": False, \"version\": \"\", \"vhosts\": []}\n                bin_path = shutil.which(\"nginx\") or (\"/usr/sbin/nginx\" if os.path.exists(\"/usr/sbin/nginx\") else None)\n                if not bin_path:\n                    return res\n                res[\"installed\"] = True\n\n                # Check version\n                v_out = subprocess.run([bin_path, \"-v\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                v_str = (v_out.stderr or v_out.stdout).strip()\n                res[\"version\"] = v_str.replace(\"nginx version: \", \"\")\n\n                # Check active\n                act = subprocess.run([\"systemctl\", \"is-active\", \"nginx\"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()\n                res[\"active\"] = (act == \"active\")\n                if not res[\"active\"]:\n                    return res\n\n                # Get configuration dump\n                dump_res = subprocess.run([bin_path, \"-T\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                out = dump_res.stdout if dump_res.returncode == 0 else \"\"\n\n                if not out:\n                    conf_files = []\n                    for d in [\"/etc/nginx/sites-enabled\", \"/etc/nginx/conf.d\"]:\n                        if os.path.isdir(d):\n                            for root, _, files in os.walk(d):\n                                for f in files:\n                                    conf_files.append(os.path.join(root, f))\n                    for cf in conf_files:\n                        try:\n                            with open(cf, \"r\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n                                out += f\"\\n# configuration file {cf}:\\n\" + f.read()\n                        except Exception:\n                            pass\n\n                # Tokenize server blocks\n                clean_lines = []\n                current_file = \"/etc/nginx/nginx.conf\"\n                for line in out.splitlines():\n                    m_file = re.match(r\"^# configuration file (.*?):\", line)\n                    if m_file:\n                        current_file = m_file.group(1).strip()\n                        clean_lines.append(f\"__FILE_MARKER__ {current_file}\")\n                        continue\n                    line_clean = re.sub(r\"#.*$\", \"\", line)\n                    if line_clean.strip():\n                        clean_lines.append(line_clean)\n\n                full_text = \"\\n\".join(clean_lines)\n                server_matches = re.finditer(r\"server\\s*\\{([^\\{\\}]*(?:\\{[^\\{\\}]*\\}[^\\{\\}]*)*)\\}\", full_text, re.DOTALL)\n                for sm in server_matches:\n                    block = sm.group(1)\n                    preceding = full_text[:sm.start()]\n                    file_matches = re.findall(r\"__FILE_MARKER__ ([^\\n]+)\", preceding)\n                    source_file = file_matches[-1] if file_matches else \"/etc/nginx/nginx.conf\"\n\n                    names = []\n                    for n in re.findall(r\"server_name\\s+([^;]+);\", block):\n                        for part in n.split():\n                            if part and part != \"_\":\n                                names.append(part)\n\n                    listens = [l.strip() for l in re.findall(r\"listen\\s+([^;]+);\", block)]\n                    certs = re.findall(r\"ssl_certificate\\s+([^;]+);\", block)\n                    keys = re.findall(r\"ssl_certificate_key\\s+([^;]+);\", block)\n\n                    ssl_cert = certs[0].strip() if certs else None\n                    ssl_key = keys[0].strip() if keys else None\n                    is_ssl = any(\"ssl\" in l or \"443\" in l for l in listens) or bool(ssl_cert)\n                    display_names = names if names else [\"_ (default / catch-all)\"]\n\n                    cert_info = inspect_cert(ssl_cert) if ssl_cert else None\n\n                    res[\"vhosts\"].append({\n                        \"webserver\": \"nginx\",\n                        \"domains\": display_names,\n                        \"ports\": listens if listens else [\"80 (default)\"],\n                        \"is_ssl\": is_ssl,\n                        \"ssl_certificate\": ssl_cert,\n                        \"ssl_key\": ssl_key,\n                        \"cert_info\": cert_info,\n                        \"config_file\": source_file\n                    })\n                return res\n\n            def parse_apache():\n                res = {\"installed\": False, \"active\": False, \"version\": \"\", \"service\": \"\", \"vhosts\": []}\n                bin_path = None\n                service_name = \"\"\n                for b, s in [(\"apache2\", \"apache2\"), (\"httpd\", \"httpd\"), (\"apachectl\", \"apache2\")]:\n                    p = shutil.which(b) or (f\"/usr/sbin/{b}\" if os.path.exists(f\"/usr/sbin/{b}\") else None)\n                    if p:\n                        bin_path = p\n                        service_name = s\n                        break\n\n                if not bin_path:\n                    return res\n                res[\"installed\"] = True\n                res[\"service\"] = service_name\n\n                # Check version\n                v_out = subprocess.run([bin_path, \"-v\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\n                v_str = (v_out.stdout or v_out.stderr).splitlines()\n                if v_str:\n                    res[\"version\"] = v_str[0].replace(\"Server version: \", \"\").strip()\n\n                # Check active\n                act = subprocess.run([\"systemctl\", \"is-active\", service_name], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()\n                res[\"active\"] = (act == \"active\")\n                if not res[\"active\"]:\n                    return res\n\n                # Parse Apache VirtualHosts\n                conf_files = []\n                for d in [\"/etc/apache2/sites-enabled\", \"/etc/apache2/conf-enabled\", \"/etc/httpd/conf.d\"]:\n                    if os.path.isdir(d):\n                        for root, _, files in os.walk(d):\n                            for f in files:\n                                if f.endswith(\".conf\"):\n                                    conf_files.append(os.path.join(root, f))\n                for f in [\"/etc/apache2/apache2.conf\", \"/etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf\"]:\n                    if os.path.isfile(f) and f not in conf_files:\n                        conf_files.append(f)\n\n                for cf in conf_files:\n                    try:\n                        with open(cf, \"r\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n                            content = f.read()\n                    except Exception:\n                        continue\n\n                    blocks = re.findall(r\"<VirtualHost\\s+([^>]+)>(.*?)</VirtualHost>\", content, re.DOTALL | re.IGNORECASE)\n                    for port, b in blocks:\n                        snames = re.findall(r\"^\\s*ServerName\\s+([^\\s#]+)\", b, re.MULTILINE | re.IGNORECASE)\n                        saliases = re.findall(r\"^\\s*ServerAlias\\s+([^\\n#]+)\", b, re.MULTILINE | re.IGNORECASE)\n                        certs = re.findall(r\"^\\s*SSLCertificateFile\\s+([^\\s#]+)\", b, re.MULTILINE | re.IGNORECASE)\n                        keys = re.findall(r\"^\\s*SSLCertificateKeyFile\\s+([^\\s#]+)\", b, re.MULTILINE | re.IGNORECASE)\n\n                        domains = []\n                        for sn in snames:\n                            domains.append(sn.strip())\n                        for sa in saliases:\n                            domains.extend(sa.split())\n\n                        ssl_cert = certs[0].strip().strip(\"\\\"'\") if certs else None\n                        ssl_key = keys[0].strip().strip(\"\\\"'\") if keys else None\n                        is_ssl = \"443\" in port or bool(ssl_cert) or bool(re.search(r\"SSLEngine\\s+on\", b, re.IGNORECASE))\n\n                        cert_info = inspect_cert(ssl_cert) if ssl_cert else None\n\n                        res[\"vhosts\"].append({\n                            \"webserver\": \"apache\",\n                            \"domains\": domains if domains else [\"_ (default / catch-all)\"],\n                            \"ports\": [port.strip()],\n                            \"is_ssl\": is_ssl,\n                            \"ssl_certificate\": ssl_cert,\n                            \"ssl_key\": ssl_key,\n                            \"cert_info\": cert_info,\n                            \"config_file\": cf\n                        })\n                return res\n\n            nginx_data = parse_nginx()\n            apache_data = parse_apache()\n\n            all_vhosts = []\n            if nginx_data[\"active\"]:\n                all_vhosts.extend(nginx_data[\"vhosts\"])\n            if apache_data[\"active\"]:\n                all_vhosts.extend(apache_data[\"vhosts\"])\n\n            unique_domains = []\n            for v in all_vhosts:\n                for d in v.get(\"domains\", []):\n                    if d not in unique_domains and d != \"_ (default / catch-all)\":\n                        unique_domains.append(d)\n\n            output = {\n                \"nginx\": nginx_data,\n                \"apache\": apache_data,\n                \"any_active\": nginx_data[\"active\"] or apache_data[\"active\"],\n                \"vhosts\": all_vhosts,\n                \"summary\": {\n                    \"total_vhosts\": len(all_vhosts),\n                    \"total_ssl_vhosts\": len([v for v in all_vhosts if v.get(\"is_ssl\")]),\n                    \"domains\": unique_domains\n                }\n            }\n            print(json.dumps(output))\n      register: raw_audit_output\n      changed_when: false\n\n    - name: Parse audit results into structured facts\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        web_audit: \"{{ raw_audit_output.stdout | from_json }}\"\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Host-Level Reporting\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    - name: Display Host Web Services & TLS Audit Report\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: |\n          ====================================================================================================\n          HOST AUDIT: {{ inventory_hostname }} ({{ ansible_host | default(ansible_default_ipv4.address | default('N/A')) }})\n          ====================================================================================================\n          * NGINX  : {{ 'INSTALLED & ACTIVE (' ~ web_audit.nginx.version ~ ')' if web_audit.nginx.active else ('INSTALLED (inactive)' if web_audit.nginx.installed else 'NOT INSTALLED') }}\n          * APACHE : {{ 'INSTALLED & ACTIVE (' ~ web_audit.apache.version ~ ')' if web_audit.apache.active else ('INSTALLED (inactive)' if web_audit.apache.installed else 'NOT INSTALLED') }}\n\n          {% if web_audit.any_active %}\n          HOSTED DOMAINS & TLS CERTIFICATES:\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          {% for v in web_audit.vhosts %}\n          [{{ loop.index }}] Web Server : {{ v.webserver | upper }}\n              Config File: {{ v.config_file }}\n              Ports      : {{ v.ports | join(', ') }}\n              Domains    : {{ v.domains | join(', ') }}\n              SSL / TLS  : {{ 'ENABLED' if v.is_ssl else 'DISABLED (Plain HTTP)' }}\n              {% if v.ssl_certificate %}\n              Cert Path  : {{ v.ssl_certificate }}\n              Key Path   : {{ v.ssl_key | default('N/A') }}\n                {% if v.cert_info and v.cert_info.exists %}\n              Status     : {{ v.cert_info.status }}\n              Subject    : {{ v.cert_info.subject }}\n              Issuer     : {{ v.cert_info.issuer }}\n              Expires    : {{ v.cert_info.expires }}\n              SANs       : {{ v.cert_info.sans | join(', ') if v.cert_info.sans else 'None' }}\n                {% else %}\n              Status     : FILE NOT FOUND ON TARGET DISK\n                {% endif %}\n              {% else %}\n              Cert Path  : None (Plain HTTP virtualhost)\n              {% endif %}\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          {% endfor %}\n          {% else %}\n          >>> NO ACTIVE WEB SERVER FOUND ON THIS HOST <<<\n          Neither Nginx nor Apache/HTTPD is currently running.\n          ====================================================================================================\n          {% endif %}\n\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Consolidated Infrastructure Summary Table\n    # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    - name: Display Consolidated Infrastructure Summary Table\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: |\n          ================================================================================================================================================================\n          INFRASTRUCTURE WEB & TLS CERTIFICATE SUMMARY TABLE\n          ================================================================================================================================================================\n          {{ '%-20s' | format('HOST') }} | {{ '%-8s' | format('SERVER') }} | {{ '%-35s' | format('HOSTED DOMAIN(S)') }} | {{ '%-12s' | format('PORT(S)') }} | {{ '%-38s' | format('TLS CERTIFICATE PATH') }} | {{ '%-24s' | format('STATUS / EXPIRY') }}\n          ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n          {% for h in ansible_play_hosts_all | sort %}\n          {% set hv = hostvars[h] %}\n          {% set wa = hv.web_audit | default({}) %}\n          {% if wa.any_active | default(false) %}\n          {% for v in wa.vhosts | default([]) %}\n          {% set c_stat = (v.cert_info.status if (v.cert_info is defined and v.cert_info.exists) else ('No TLS' if not v.ssl_certificate else 'FILE NOT FOUND')) %}\n          {{ '%-20s' | format(h) }} | {{ '%-8s' | format(v.webserver) }} | {{ '%-35s' | format(v.domains | join(', ') | truncate(35, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-12s' | format(v.ports | join(',') | truncate(12, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-38s' | format(v.ssl_certificate | default('None') | truncate(38, True, '...')) }} | {{ '%-24s' | format(c_stat | truncate(24, True, '...')) }}\n          {% endfor %}\n          {% else %}\n          {{ '%-20s' | format(h) }} | {{ '%-8s' | format('N/A') }} | {{ '%-35s' | format('No active web server') }} | {{ '%-12s' | format('N/A') }} | {{ '%-38s' | format('None') }} | {{ '%-24s' | format('INACTIVE / NO SERVICE') }}\n          {% endif %}\n          {% endfor %}\n          ================================================================================================================================================================\n      run_once: true\n      delegate_to: localhost\nEOF","Cwd":"/home/koby/LINUX","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Create audit-web-certs.yml playbook"}}]}
