{"step_index":491,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-17T11:53:43Z","content":"The playbook [`playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml`](file:///home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml) has been crafted, tested, and validated end-to-end against live infrastructure (`mtq-mailsrvp-01`).\n\n---\n\n### Architecture & Execution Flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"ansible-playbook playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml\"] --> B[\"Phase 1: import_playbook: bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml\"]\n    B --> C[\"SSHD inspection & AllowGroups check\"]\n    C --> D[\"User koby-bowser-ansible & Passwordless Sudo (/etc/sudoers.d)\"]\n    D --> E[\"Deploy SSH Public Key (~/.ssh/authorized_keys & centralized path)\"]\n    E --> F[\"Phase 2: Web Server & TLS Discovery Engine\"]\n    F --> G[\"Detect Installation & Active State (Nginx / Apache2 / HTTPD)\"]\n    G --> H[\"Extract VirtualHosts, Hosted Domains, Listening Ports\"]\n    H --> I[\"Resolve On-Disk TLS Cert Paths & Parse Expiry / SANs via OpenSSL\"]\n    I --> J[\"Per-Host Detailed Audit Cards\"]\n    I --> K[\"Consolidated Multi-Host Infrastructure Summary Table\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n### Playbook Highlights\n\n1. **Phase 1 Bootstrap Integration**:\n   - Uses `ansible.builtin.import_playbook: bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml` as the first play.\n   - Automatically handles Debian/CentOS quirks, dynamic `AllowGroups` discovery (e.g. `SSH_Users`), centralized vs. local `authorized_keys`, and passwordless sudo.\n\n2. **Phase 2 Non-Destructive Deep Inspection**:\n   - Embedded self-contained Python discovery engine running under `become: true`.\n   - **Nginx inspection**: parses live dump (`nginx -T`) and filesystem configs (`/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/*`, `/etc/nginx/conf.d/*`), extracting `server_name`, `listen` directives, `ssl_certificate`, and `ssl_certificate_key`.\n   - **Apache / HTTPD inspection**: parses VirtualHost blocks across `/etc/apache2/sites-enabled/*` and `/etc/httpd/conf.d/*`, extracting `ServerName`, `ServerAlias`, `SSLCertificateFile`, and `SSLCertificateKeyFile`.\n   - **Certificate Deep Dive**: runs `openssl x509` against every on-disk certificate to extract expiration dates, days remaining, Subject CN, Issuer, and Subject Alternative Names (SANs).\n\n3. **Dual-Layer Output Reporting**:\n   - **Host-level card**: Detailed breakdown per host with clear separation between plain HTTP and SSL/TLS virtualhosts.\n   - **Consolidated table**: High-level cross-infrastructure summary table aligned across all hosts in the play.\n\n---\n\n### Live Verification Output (`mtq-mailsrvp-01` / `172.30.39.153:30`)\n\n#### 1. Per-Host Detailed Report\n```text\n====================================================================================================\nHOST AUDIT: 172.30.39.153 (172.30.39.153)\n====================================================================================================\n* NGINX  : INSTALLED & ACTIVE (nginx/1.26.3)\n* APACHE : INSTALLED (inactive)\n\nHOSTED DOMAINS & TLS CERTIFICATES:\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[1] Web Server : NGINX\n    Config File: /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default\n    Ports      : 80 default_server, [::]:80 default_server\n    Domains    : _ (default / catch-all)\n    SSL / TLS  : DISABLED (Plain HTTP)\n        Cert Path  : None (Plain HTTP virtualhost)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2] Web Server : NGINX\n    Config File: /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/roundcube.conf\n    Ports      : 80\n    Domains    : 172.30.39.153, postfix.outremer-telecom.fr\n    SSL / TLS  : DISABLED (Plain HTTP)\n        Cert Path  : None (Plain HTTP virtualhost)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[3] Web Server : NGINX\n    Config File: /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/roundcube.conf\n    Ports      : 443 ssl\n    Domains    : 172.30.39.153, po